infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title What actually stops the stale write
  desc Four proposed fixes for split-brain — only one closes the window
  compares
    - label Fencing token (closes the window)
      children
        - label Resource enforces order
          desc Storage rejects any write whose token is below the highest it has seen
        - label Clock-independent
          desc Correctness no longer depends on the paused node noticing it lost the lease
        - label Token 33 loses to 34
          desc Paused leader's lower token is fenced off at the resource boundary
    - label The three that leave it open
      children
        - label Shorten the lease TTL
          desc A paused process can't give up a lease it doesn't know expired — window shrinks, never closes
        - label Self-check before write
          desc During a GC pause no code runs, so there is no moment to check the clock
        - label Faster consensus
          desc Speeds election but is orthogonal — the deposed leader still wakes and writes stale
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f43f5e
